    kind: work_item  # fb45
    title: "def/use records NOTHING inside statements it already matched: Go grouped var declarations and defer, Python subscript indices — the omission is inside a COVERED extent so no coverage gate can see it (INV-lupav L4, reproduced)"  # fb45
    status: todo_hard  # fb45
    priority: 2  # fb45
    parent:  # fb45
    tags:  # fb45
    - taint  # fb45
    - adr_0017  # fb45
    - dataflow  # fb45
    isbefore: []  # fb45
    duplicate_of: []  # fb45
    not_duplicate_of: []  # fb45
    pr_ref:  # fb45
    description: "INV-lupav's clause L4, REPRODUCED. It was recorded on that thread as\n\"structural and UNDEMONSTRATED\" on 2026-09-14; this is the demonstration, found\nby a mechanical sweep rather than by guessing shapes.\n\nWHY THIS CLASS IS DIFFERENT FROM WI-losod, AND WHY IT IS WORSE. WI-losod's\nconstructs (Go if/for initializers, range clauses) leave an UNCOVERED region,\nso WI-joluk's coverage gate -- widened by WI-mugop to semantic leaves -- detects\nthem and forfeits refutation. These constructs are recorded as a statement and\nthe extractor then fills it with NOTHING. There is no uncovered region, so no\ncoverage predicate at any width can see the omission. The gate fails SAFE on\nWI-losod's class and is BLIND to this one.\n\nTHREE SHAPES, TWO LANGUAGES, each read back against source.\n\n1. GO GROUPED VAR DECLARATION. alertmanager api/v2/api.go:251, live:\n       var (\n           receiverFilter *regexp.Regexp\n           res = open_api_models.GettableAlerts{}\n           logger = api.requestLogger(params.HTTPRequest)\n       )\n   recorded as ONE statement:\n       line 251  var_declaration  defines=[] uses=[]\n   Three definitions and a call argument, none recorded.\n\n2. GO DEFER. Both nodes at the line record nothing:\n       line 4  deferred_call    defines=[] uses=[]\n       line 4  defer_statement  defines=[] uses=[]\n   so the use of the deferred callee and of its arguments is invisible.\n   `defer log.Printf(\"%s\", tainted)` is an ordinary shape, not a contrived one.\n\n3. PYTHON SUBSCRIPT INDEX. `counters[key] = 1` records\n       line 4  assignment  defines=['counters'] uses=[]\n   The index `key` is not a use. Dominant shape in the python sweep.\n\nIT PRODUCES AN UNEARNED False, WHICH IS THE POINT. Fixture through the\nproduction path, control first, both functions walkable:\n\n    CONTROL (msg := cwd, use recorded)   -> True    ADMISSIBLE\n    L4      (var block, use unrecorded)  -> False   <- true answer is True\n\n    l4leak    walkable=True  forfeited=False   <- gate silent\n    l4covered walkable=True  forfeited=False\n    edges in l4leak   : cwd 13->14, a 14->15          (chain to sink GONE)\n    edges in l4covered: cwd 23->24, a 24->25, cwd 23->26, msg 26->27\n\nOne variable changed -- `var ( msg = cwd )` against `msg := cwd` -- and the\nwhole taint chain to the sink disappears from the DDG while the function still\nreports fully covered. Since WI-kabif (2026-09-02) that False REMOVES the flow.\n\nPOPULATION, from the sweep (instrument:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/taint-area-08052026/meas/use_completeness_sweep.py,\ncontrol passing, candidates attributed to the INNERMOST recorded statement):\n    alertmanager/go   2580 functions   370 candidate misses\n    hypergumbo/python 35083 functions 1622 candidate misses\nThese are CANDIDATES, not findings: shadowing, a field sharing a local's name\nand struct-literal keys survive the known-local filter. The three shapes above\nare the ones read back to source and confirmed. Nobody should quote 370 or 1622\nas a defect count.\n\nCROSS-LANGUAGE BY DIFFERENT SHAPES, which is WI-joluk's own argument arriving\nagain: go fails on var groups and defer, python on subscript indices. A remedy\nwritten from either language alone ships with the other invisible.\n\nREMEDY IS EXTRACTOR-LEVEL, not gate-level, and that is the finding. A coverage\npredicate compares AST nodes to recorded statement EXTENTS; it can establish\nthat a statement was recorded, never that its contents were accounted for. If\nINV-lupav is to close, either these extractors record what is inside the\nstatements they already match, or the walk needs a completeness signal that is\nnot coverage-shaped -- for instance the extractor reporting, per statement,\nthat it understood the construct rather than merely visited it."  # fb45
    fields: {}  # fb45
- op: discuss  # 0e56
  at: '2026-09-15T01:59:16Z'  # 0e56
  by: agent  # 0e56
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0e56
  clock: 2  # 0e56
  nonce: '0e56'  # 0e56
  message: "CLOSED. The clause reproduces, the filed remedy does not survive measurement, and one of\nthe three filed shapes does not reproduce at all. All three corrections are below, ahead\nof the fix, because two of them are mine.\n\nSHAPE 2 (Go defer) DOES NOT REPRODUCE AT TIP, AND THE FILING IS WRONG ABOUT IT. Re-run,\none variable, four defer forms plus two controls:\n\n    defer selector call     accounts_for_t=True   defer_statement uses=(log, t)\n    defer plain call        accounts_for_t=True   defer_statement uses=(t,)\n    defer method on local   accounts_for_t=True   defer_statement uses=(t,)\n    defer func literal      accounts_for_t=True   defer_statement uses=(t,)\n    go stmt (control)       accounts_for_t=True\n    plain call (control)    accounts_for_t=True\n\nThe fallback collector reads the use correctly on the OUTER defer_statement. The empty\ndeferred_call I filed sits INSIDE it, at the same line, and accounts for nothing --\nwhich is harmless, because a sibling that genuinely did read the value is not the\n\"recorded sibling vouches for an unrecorded one\" shape #957 closed. I read an empty\nbucket in isolation and called it a defect. That is landmine 5 (CHECK THE BUCKET THAT\nCAME BACK EMPTY) firing on me in the flattering direction.\n\nSHAPES 1 AND 3 REPRODUCE, AND A SWEEP FOUND FOUR MORE. Four languages, controls in each,\neach case classified by whether WI-joluk's widened gate already sees it:\n\n    GATE BLIND (this clause)          go grouped var (two forms)\n                                      py subscript index, aug subscript, slice index,\n                                         del c[t]\n                                      ts template substitution\n    GATE SEES IT (fails safe)         py with open(t), ts for..of, rust for..in\n    rust                              no instance in the sample\n\nCross-language by DIFFERENT shapes, which was the filing's own argument and holds.\n\nTHE PROPOSED REMEDY IS REFUTED, AND THE SWEEP IS WHAT REFUTES IT. This item proposed a\nper-statement \"I understood this construct\" signal -- enumerate what the extractor\nHANDLES, forfeit the rest. In SIX OF THE SEVEN shapes the handler IS registered for the\nnode type and is merely incomplete: go var_declaration is in _HANDLERS and returns\nnothing for the grouped form, python assignment is in _HANDLERS and returns\ndefines=[c] uses=[] for c[key]=1. A flag keyed on dispatch-table membership would have\nclaimed understanding in all six. MEMBERSHIP IN A DISPATCH TABLE IS NOT EVIDENCE THE\nDISPATCH WAS COMPLETE.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED INSTEAD is structural and self-differential: cfg.unaccounted_names diffs\neach recorded statement defines/uses against the semantic leaves inside its own extent,\nreusing _is_semantic_leaf so \"worth accounting for\" keeps ONE spelling with the coverage\ngate. No per-language vocabulary to keep in step -- the same argument that chose the\nstructural predicate in WI-mugop.\n\nTWO DESIGN POINTS THAT WERE NOT OBVIOUS AND ARE LOAD-BEARING.\n  (a) A name is accounted for by ANY ENCLOSING recorded statement, not the innermost.\n      Innermost attribution reports the empty deferred_call above and flags a variable\n      the extractor did follow. My earlier sweep instrument had the opposite bug\n      (attributing to EVERY enclosing statement) and I over-corrected to innermost.\n  (b) PER VARIABLE, NOT PER FUNCTION, so the walk ESCAPES rather than forfeiting.\n      Coverage is a property of a function; this is a property of a value. A function\n      forfeit would withhold False from every walk over it rather than from the walks\n      carrying the unaccounted value.\n\nFLOOR CHECK BEFORE WIRING, corpus roots NAMED (forfeit_share.log records names not\npaths, and that cost a whole false-alarm regression):\n\n    ~/repos/alertmanager   go       12.6% of functions, 4.8% of tracked names\n    ~/hypergumbo           python    4.9% of functions, 2.1% of tracked names\n\nSo False stays reachable for the large majority, and the spelling that fires everywhere\n-- the one the WI-mugop floor check killed -- is ruled out by measurement.\n\nBLAST RADIUS MEASURED AND ZERO, REPORTED AS ZERO. Paired arms, the real walk called\ntwice on identical inputs:\n\n    hypergumbo-core own claims   84 walks   34 handed a signal   2 raised   0 moved\n    ~/repos/alertmanager generic 22 walks    8 handed a signal   1 raised   0 moved\n\nZero because section 3a returns False zero times on either repo. Same picture as #957\nand for the same reason."  # 0e56
